repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/krishna-2-005/Agentic-AI-Logistics-Control-Tower
url: https://control-tower-mu-rouge.vercel.app
abstract: >-
  The OSRM route estimate recorded in Delhivery's public trip data runs
  short almost every time: 98.3% of 26,369 origin-destination legs run over
  it and the median leg takes 2.0 times the estimate. This repository
  localises where that error concentrates and says how confidently. A Welch
  audit with false-discovery control flags 273 corridors as slower than the
  network, but legs of one recurring service are correlated and the same
  procedure on placebo data returns about 680 discoveries; a cluster-aware
  permutation test confirms none at its pre-registered strictness, while
  corridor effects persist between halves of the period. A gradient-boosted
  residual over a hierarchical back-off baseline reaches 29.66 minutes mean
  absolute error against the baseline's 32.39 (day-block 95% interval for
  the difference -3.41 to -2.11), with the gain on corridors without
  history; the Spark model that the streaming job serves scores 30.90. The
  repository also reports two evaluation pitfalls (an optimiser default that
  disabled the chosen loss, and a replay that leaked future history into an
  alert precision) and a measured, deterministic-core agent layer. Every
  number is generated from a frozen results file.
keywords:
  - big data
  - apache spark
  - logistics
  - travel time prediction
  - route auditing
  - false discovery rate
  - empirical bayes
  - llm agents
  - stream processing
